  ["R1-10", "Claims of preventing starvation and preserving fairness exceed the evidence, since the utility\u2013fairness coefficient can reach 1 and selection does not guarantee meaningful aggregation influence.", "Overreaching language in the Conclusion is scoped to what is shown (Replacement 18). Selection-frequency distributions, maximum waiting times, and cumulative aggregation influence per client are not available without the original logs; this is disclosed explicitly (Replacement 22, item 4) rather than asserted.", "disclosed"],
