413	Equation (11) defines the adaptive reference convergence rate $\Omega^t$, which guides the control signal to balance exploitation and exploration. Here, $\rho_{\text{base}}^t$ represents the convergence rate obtained from a prior run of a standard baseline model or state-of-the-art algorithm under identical experimental conditions, and $\gamma$ denotes an acceleration index.
