415	Client-side uncertainty is introduced into the fitness score as a variance based penalty term. It quantifies KL estimate across several small batches of local client’s dataset. This term penalizes the clients whose data is highly unstable or non-representative data (i.e., high variance), even having a high utility as its variability between samples indicates that the data might be noisy or contain extreme outliers. While the clients with low uncertainty score reflect their stability that enhances robustness and stability under heterogeneous scenarios. The uncertainty penalty term for client \textit{i} is defined as:
